#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""cc-docs — the document register: numbers, stamps and files every PDF the box finishes for its owner.

A number is PPP-NNNN-R. PPP is the project, given the next free number in its range the first time a document is
filed under it (work 001-099, course 101-199, member 901-999); NNNN, four digits, is the document within the project, in filing
order; R is the revision, A for the first finished version and the next letter for each finished version whose
content differs from the last (I and O are skipped, and after Z comes AA). A filed copy is named
`PPP-NNNN-R_<slug>.pdf`, is written once, read-only, and never rewritten.

    cc-docs file <pdf> --project <name|PPP> --title <t> [--source <path>] [--no-stamp]
                 [--kind work|course|member] [--member <handle>] [--date YYYY-MM-DD]
                 [--describes PCB-NNNN-R] [--note <text>] [--cost <step>=<usd>]…
        Called by a maker at the end of a finished build. The same source path, or else the same title in the same
        project, is the same document. Content unchanged since the current revision files nothing and prints that
        revision; otherwise the next letter is filed. A PDF whose text carries no number gets a small grey stamp
        `PPP-NNNN-R · 24 Sep 2026` bottom-left on every page; one that already carries its own number (a LaTeX build
        that took it from `number`) is filed as it is; one carrying a different number is refused. --no-stamp is for
        a document that must not show a number (a resume, anything going outside): it is kept on the document, so its
        later revisions are not stamped either. A new project needs --kind, --member (a member project, visible to
        that member's workspace and the owner) or a project created first with `project`. Prints `<number>\t<path>` and whether
        it filed or found the content unchanged. The rest is recorded on the revision it files, and nothing is recorded
        when nothing is filed: --describes the board revision a document is about (a board's part number, PCB-0001-B),
        which the stamp then carries too, as `002-0012-A · PCB-0001-B · 24 Sep 2026`; --note a line on what changed;
        --cost, once per step, what the maker spent generating it in US dollars (`--cost draft=0.80 --cost review=0.43`).
    cc-docs number --project <name|PPP> --title <t> [--source <path>] [--describes PCB-NNNN-R] [--tex]
        The number `file` would give a changed build of this document now, for a build that prints its own footer:
        plain, or with --tex as `\\def\\docnumber{…}\\def\\docstamp{… · 24 Sep 2026}` to \\input before compiling.
        It reserves nothing, and a build whose content turns out unchanged is not filed.
    cc-docs project <name> [--number PPP] [--kind work|course|member] [--member <handle>]
        Create a project (at PPP, or the next free number in its kind's range), or print an existing one.
    cc-docs find <PPP-NNNN | PPP-NNNN-R | words…>
        The file of a document's current revision (or of the exact revision named), found by number, title or
        words in the title, project name or source path. Several equally good matches are listed to stderr, exit 3;
        none, exit 1.
    cc-docs list [--project <name|PPP>]
        One line per document: number of the current revision, date, visibility, title.
    cc-docs star <PPP-NNNN> on|off [--viewer owner|<workspace id>]
        Star or unstar a document for one viewer (the owner by default). Stars are per viewer, and a viewer can
        star only a document visible to it.
    cc-docs public <PPP-NNNN-R> on|off
        On gives that one revision a public link: an unguessable token, printed, kept while it stays public (on
        again prints the same one). Off deletes the token for good, so the old link never works again and on
        afterwards mints a different one. The register's owner runs this; nobody else may.
    cc-docs token <token> <PPP-NNNN-R>
        The filed copy a public link serves: printed only when the token is that revision's, exit 1 otherwise.
    cc-docs library --viewer owner|<workspace id>
        Everything that viewer may see, as JSON: projects, documents, per-viewer star, and per revision its date,
        note, file, pages, bytes, board revision and cost. The owner sees the whole register and each public
        revision's token; a member sees only documents visible to its workspace, its own stars, and no tokens.
        Any other viewer is refused.
    cc-docs member <handle> [--files <dir>]
        The host's half of filing from inside a member workspace, run by the Slack daemon for its member verb `docs`
        (below): one ask as JSON on stdin, {"ok", "text"|"error"} on stdout. Nobody else calls it.
    cc-docs fold <keep PPP-NNNN> <other PPP-NNNN>…
        Makes the other documents revisions of <keep>, for old versions filed as documents of their own. Every revision
        of them all is ordered oldest first by date (ties by the order given) with <keep>'s current revision last, so
        the next build of its source still matches it, and relettered A, B, C…; refused when another revision is dated
        after it. <keep> keeps its title, source, visibility and stars. The filed copies are renamed to match (their
        bytes, and any stamp printed in them, are not rewritten), a revision whose number changed loses its public
        link, and the other numbers are retired. All must be in one project, none with a retired revision. Prints
        `<old number>\t<new number>\t<path>` per revision.
    cc-docs retire <PPP-NNNN | PPP-NNNN-R>
        Takes a document (or one revision; its last revision retires the document) out of the register, its member
        views and its public link, for a document filed by mistake. Its filed copies move under retired/files/.
    cc-docs selfcheck

INSIDE A MEMBER WORKSPACE (CC_MEMBER_SANDBOX=1) the register is that member's read-only view, so `file` and `number`
cross the workspace's own socket (~/.cc/slack/sock inside) as the daemon's member verb `docs`, the way `cc-mail send`
does, and print the host's line. --project may be left out there. The host files under the workspace's own member
project: the one the ask names when it is that member's, else that member's first, else a new one named after the
handle. It takes the handle from the socket and never from the ask; refuses another member's project or --member,
a PDF or --source outside the workspace's own trees (~/dev/<h>, its track worktrees, its Slack files), a file that
is not a PDF, and one over 64 MiB; reads the PDF from one fd so it cannot be swapped between the check and the
read; and ignores --kind. A project an owner's maker names that is not the member's files under the member's own
instead, so a build that sets DOC_PROJECT still files. `project`, `star`, `public`, `token`, `fold` and `retire` are
refused inside.

THE REGISTER is one JSON file, $CC_DOCS_ROOT/register.json (default ~/.cc/documents), with the filed copies under
files/PPP/ beside it: private state, in no repo, and outside cc-lib's own tree (cc-lib indexes the register). Per
document it holds number, title, project, source, visibility (the owner, or the owner and one member), who starred
it (starred_by, viewer ids), and per revision the letter, file, date, the PDF it was filed from, a content
fingerprint, and when given the note, board revision, cost and public token. The
fingerprint hashes the PDF's text with any document stamp taken out together with every page rendered small and grey
with its bottom strip (stamp, footer) cut off, so a rebuild that changes only a figure is a new revision and one that
differs only in its stamp, footer or bytes is unchanged; a PDF neither can read falls back to its bytes. A revision
filed with the older text-only print still matches an unchanged rebuild. Writes hold a lock and replace the file whole.

VISIBILITY is keyed by workspace id, the one cc-lib keys its indexes by (~/.cc/members/<handle>/workspace-id, minted
by cc-sandbox or cc-lib, never here): a member project records its member's id, and each of its documents is visible
to ["owner", <id>]. The owner sees the whole register. A member workspace gets a VIEW, ws/<id>/ under the root, and
never the register itself: a register of the same shape holding only the documents that name its id, with their
filed copies hard-linked beside it, so `CC_DOCS_ROOT=<the view> cc-docs find …` works inside it unchanged. `file`
rewrites the views its document reaches after every filing, in place (a bind mount of the directory keeps seeing
them), so the directory can be mounted read-only into that member's sandbox the way cc-lib mounts ws/<id>/. A
star or a public switch rewrites them too. A view never carries a public token.

RETIRED numbers (`fold`, `retire`) are kept in the register's `retired`, and a retired revision's letter in its
document's `retired_revs`, so neither is handed out again. What either verb takes out of the register is kept as
retired/<number>.json beside it, and nothing is deleted.
"""
import datetime
import fcntl
import hashlib
import json
import os
import re
import secrets
import shutil
import stat
import subprocess
import sys
import tempfile

ROOT = os.environ.get("CC_DOCS_ROOT") or os.path.join(os.path.expanduser("~"), ".cc", "documents")
MEMBERS = os.path.join(os.path.expanduser("~"), ".cc", "members")
RANGES = {"work": (1, 99), "course": (101, 199), "member": (901, 999)}
LETTERS = "ABCDEFGHJKLMNPQRSTUVWXYZ"   # I and O are skipped: they read like 1 and 0
NUM = re.compile(r"^(\d{3})-(\d{4})(?:-([A-HJ-NP-Z]{1,3}))?$")
BOARD = re.compile(r"^PCB-\d{4}-[A-HJ-NP-Z]{1,3}$")   # a board's part number and hardware revision
STAMP = re.compile(r"\b\d{3}-\d{4}-[A-HJ-NP-Z]{1,3}\b(?:\s*·\s*PCB-\d{4}-[A-HJ-NP-Z]{1,3}\b)?"
                   r"(?:\s*·\s*\d{1,2} [A-Z][a-z]{2} \d{4})?")
STEP = re.compile(r"^[a-z0-9][a-z0-9_-]{0,39}$")
WID = re.compile(r"^[0-9a-f]{16}$")
STOP = set("a an the of for and or to in on my me get find doc document pdf".split())


class Refused(Exception):
    pass


def letter(i):
    """0 -> A, 23 -> Z, 24 -> AA: bijective base 24 over LETTERS."""
    s = ""
    i += 1
    while i:
        i, r = divmod(i - 1, len(LETTERS))
        s = LETTERS[r] + s
    return s


def slugify(t):
    return re.sub(r"[^a-z0-9]+", "-", t.lower()).strip("-")[:60].strip("-") or "document"


def stampdate(d):
    return f"{d.day} {d.strftime('%b %Y')}"


# ── the register ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
def regpath():
    return os.path.join(ROOT, "register.json")


def load():
    try:
        with open(regpath()) as f:
            return json.load(f)
    except FileNotFoundError:
        return {"version": 1, "projects": {}, "documents": {}}


def save(reg):
    fd, tmp = tempfile.mkstemp(dir=ROOT, prefix=".register.")
    with os.fdopen(fd, "w") as f:
        json.dump(reg, f, indent=1, sort_keys=True)
        f.write("\n")
    os.replace(tmp, regpath())


class Lock:
    def __enter__(self):
        os.makedirs(ROOT, mode=0o700, exist_ok=True)
        self.f = open(os.path.join(ROOT, ".lock"), "w")
        fcntl.flock(self.f, fcntl.LOCK_EX)
        return self

    def __exit__(self, *a):
        self.f.close()


def find_project(reg, name):
    if re.fullmatch(r"\d{3}", name or ""):
        return name if name in reg["projects"] else None
    for p, d in reg["projects"].items():
        if d["name"].lower() == (name or "").lower():
            return p
    return None


def make_project(reg, name, number=None, kind=None, member=None):
    """-> PPP, existing or new. A new one takes --number, or the next free number in its kind's range."""
    p = find_project(reg, number or name)
    if p:
        if number and reg["projects"][p]["name"].lower() != name.lower():
            raise Refused(f"project {p} is already {reg['projects'][p]['name']!r}")
        return p
    if find_project(reg, name):
        raise Refused(f"project {name!r} already has number {find_project(reg, name)}")
    if member:
        kind = kind or "member"
    if number:
        n = int(number)
        kind = kind or next((k for k, (a, b) in RANGES.items() if a <= n <= b), None)
        if kind not in RANGES or not RANGES[kind][0] <= n <= RANGES[kind][1]:
            raise Refused(f"project number {number} is outside the {kind or 'known'} ranges")
    elif kind in RANGES:
        a, b = RANGES[kind]
        n = next((i for i in range(a, b + 1) if f"{i:03d}" not in reg["projects"]), None)
        if n is None:
            raise Refused(f"the {kind} range is full")
    else:
        raise Refused(f"no project {name!r}: give --kind work|course|member, --member or --number to create it")
    if kind == "member" and not member:
        raise Refused("a member project needs --member <handle>: it is visible to that member and the owner")
    p = f"{n:03d}"
    reg["projects"][p] = {"name": name, "kind": kind, "member": member if kind == "member" else None,
                          "workspace": workspace_id(member) if kind == "member" else None,
                          "created": datetime.date.today().isoformat()}
    return p


def workspace_id(handle):
    """A member's workspace id, as cc-lib reads it: 16 hex in a regular file. None of it is minted here."""
    f = os.path.join(MEMBERS, handle, "workspace-id")
    try:
        wid = "" if os.path.islink(f) else open(f).read().strip()
    except OSError:
        wid = ""
    if not re.fullmatch(r"[0-9a-f]{16}", wid):
        raise Refused(f"member {handle!r} has no workspace id at {f}; its workspace must exist before its documents")
    return wid


def write_views(reg, ids):
    """Each workspace id in ids gets ws/<id>/: a register of the documents visible to it, and their files linked in."""
    for wid in sorted(ids):
        v = os.path.join(ROOT, "ws", wid)
        os.makedirs(v, mode=0o700, exist_ok=True)
        # a view never carries a public token: only the owner can see or kill a public link
        docs = {n: dict(d, revisions=[{k: v for k, v in r.items() if k != "public_token"} for r in d["revisions"]])
                for n, d in reg["documents"].items() if wid in d.get("visibility", ())}
        for d in docs.values():
            for r in d["revisions"]:
                dst = os.path.join(v, r["file"])
                if not os.path.exists(dst):
                    os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(dst), exist_ok=True)
                    os.link(os.path.join(ROOT, r["file"]), dst)
        view = {"version": reg["version"], "documents": docs,
                "projects": {p: reg["projects"][p] for p in sorted({d["project"] for d in docs.values()})}}
        fd, tmp = tempfile.mkstemp(dir=v, prefix=".register.")
        with os.fdopen(fd, "w") as f:
            json.dump(view, f, indent=1, sort_keys=True)
            f.write("\n")
        os.replace(tmp, os.path.join(v, "register.json"))


def match_doc(reg, proj, title, source):
    """The same source path, else the same title in the same project, is the same document.
    Brief: "same source path or title = same document"."""
    if source:
        for num, d in reg["documents"].items():
            if d.get("source") == source:
                if proj and d["project"] != proj:
                    raise Refused(f"{source} is already {num}, under project {d['project']}, not {proj}")
                return num
    for num, d in reg["documents"].items():
        if d["project"] == proj and d["title"].lower() == title.lower():
            return num
    return None


def next_doc(reg, proj):
    used = [int(n.split("-")[1]) for n, d in reg["documents"].items() if d["project"] == proj]
    used += [int(n.split("-")[1]) for n in reg.get("retired", {}) if n.startswith(proj + "-")]   # never handed out again
    return f"{proj}-{max(used, default=0) + 1:04d}"


def current(d):
    return d["revisions"][-1] if d["revisions"] else None


# ── the PDF ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
def pdftext(path):
    r = subprocess.run(["pdftotext", "-q", path, "-"], capture_output=True, text=True)
    if r.returncode != 0:
        raise Refused(f"{path}: pdftotext could not read it ({r.stderr.strip()[:200]})")
    return r.stdout


def textprint(text):
    """The text-only fingerprint the first register was filed with, or None for a PDF with no text."""
    body = " ".join(STAMP.sub(" ", text).split())
    return "text:" + hashlib.sha256(body.encode()).hexdigest() if body else None


def pageprint(path):
    """A hash of every page rendered small and grey with its bottom strip cut off, where a stamp or a footer sits,
    so a changed figure changes it and a changed stamp does not. None when the pages cannot be rendered."""
    with tempfile.TemporaryDirectory(prefix="cc-docs-fp-") as t:
        r = subprocess.run(["pdftoppm", "-r", "36", "-gray", path, os.path.join(t, "p")], capture_output=True)
        names = sorted(os.listdir(t), key=lambda x: int(re.sub(r"\D", "", x) or 0))
        if r.returncode != 0 or not names:
            return None
        h = hashlib.sha256()
        for name in names:
            with open(os.path.join(t, name), "rb") as f:
                m = re.match(rb"P5\s+(\d+)\s+(\d+)\s+\d+\s", f.read(64))
                if not m:
                    return None
                f.seek(m.end())
                w, rows = int(m.group(1)), int(m.group(2))
                h.update(f.read(w * (rows - rows * 12 // 100)))
        return h.hexdigest()


def fingerprint(path, text):
    """Text and page images together; a PDF neither can read falls back to its bytes."""
    body, pix = textprint(text), pageprint(path)
    if pix:
        return "page:" + hashlib.sha256(f"{body}|{pix}".encode()).hexdigest()
    if body:
        return body
    with open(path, "rb") as f:
        return "bytes:" + hashlib.sha256(f.read()).hexdigest()


def pages(path):
    r = subprocess.run(["pdfinfo", path], capture_output=True, text=True)
    m = re.search(r"^Pages:\s+(\d+)", r.stdout, re.M)
    return int(m.group(1)) if m else -1


def stamp(src, dst, text):
    """Every page of src with `text` small and grey at the bottom left, written to dst."""
    with tempfile.TemporaryDirectory(prefix="cc-docs-") as t:
        shutil.copy(src, os.path.join(t, "in.pdf"))
        tex = text.replace("·", r"\textperiodcentered{}")
        with open(os.path.join(t, "s.tex"), "w") as f:
            f.write("\\documentclass{article}\\usepackage[T1]{fontenc}\\usepackage{pdfpages}\\usepackage{xcolor}\n"
                    "\\begin{document}\\includepdf[pages=-,fitpaper,picturecommand={\\put(30,20){\\fontsize{7}{8}"
                    "\\selectfont\\sffamily\\color[gray]{0.5}" + tex + "}}]{in.pdf}\\end{document}\n")
        r = subprocess.run(["pdflatex", "-interaction=batchmode", "-halt-on-error", "s.tex"], cwd=t,
                           capture_output=True, text=True)
        out = os.path.join(t, "s.pdf")
        if r.returncode != 0 or not os.path.isfile(out) or pages(out) != pages(src):
            raise Refused(f"{src}: the stamp overlay failed (pdflatex exit {r.returncode}); nothing filed")
        shutil.copy(out, dst)


# ── commands ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
def plan(reg, a):
    """-> (proj, docnum, doc-or-None, next letter). Creates the project in reg (the caller decides to save)."""
    proj = find_project(reg, a.project)
    if not proj:
        if re.fullmatch(r"\d{3}", a.project):
            raise Refused(f"no project {a.project}: create it by name with `cc-docs project <name> --number {a.project}`")
        proj = make_project(reg, a.project, None, a.kind, a.member)
    source = os.path.abspath(a.source) if a.source else None
    num = match_doc(reg, proj, a.title, source)
    d = reg["documents"].get(num) if num else None
    return proj, num or next_doc(reg, proj), d, letter(len(d["revisions"]) + len(d.get("retired_revs", ())) if d else 0)


def cmd_file(a):
    src = os.path.abspath(a.pdf)
    shown = getattr(a, "origin", None) or a.pdf   # a member's PDF is filed from the host's copy; its own path is the one named
    if not os.path.isfile(src):
        raise Refused(f"{shown}: no such file")
    date = datetime.date.fromisoformat(a.date) if a.date else datetime.date.today()
    describes, cost = check_describes(a.describes), parse_cost(a.cost)
    text = pdftext(src)
    fp = fingerprint(src, text)
    with Lock():
        reg = load()
        proj, num, d, rev = plan(reg, a)
        # brief: "a changed finished version = next letter, unchanged content = no new letter"
        # a revision filed before page images were hashed carries a text-only print: that still counts as unchanged
        if d and current(d) and current(d)["fingerprint"] in (fp, textprint(text)):
            print(f"{num}-{current(d)['rev']}\t{os.path.join(ROOT, current(d)['file'])}\tunchanged, nothing filed")
            return 0
        full = f"{num}-{rev}"
        carried = set(m.group(0).split()[0] for m in STAMP.finditer(text))
        if carried - {full}:
            raise Refused(f"{shown} already carries {', '.join(sorted(carried - {full}))}, but it would be filed as "
                          f"{full}; rebuild it with `cc-docs number`")
        nostamp = a.no_stamp or bool(d and d.get("stamp") is False)
        rel = os.path.join("files", proj, f"{full}_{slugify(a.title)}.pdf")
        dst = os.path.join(ROOT, rel)
        if os.path.exists(dst):
            raise Refused(f"{dst} exists; a filed revision is never rewritten")
        os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(dst), exist_ok=True)
        tmp = dst + ".part"
        if nostamp:
            how = "none"
            shutil.copy(src, tmp)
        elif full in carried:
            how = "carried"
            shutil.copy(src, tmp)
        else:
            how = "overlay"
            stamp(src, tmp, " · ".join([full] + ([describes] if describes else []) + [stampdate(date)]))
        os.chmod(tmp, 0o444)
        os.replace(tmp, dst)
        with open(dst, "rb") as f:
            sha = hashlib.sha256(f.read()).hexdigest()
        if not d:
            pd = reg["projects"][proj]
            d = reg["documents"][num] = {
                "number": num, "project": proj, "title": a.title, "source": os.path.abspath(a.source) if a.source else None,
                "visibility": ["owner"] + ([pd["workspace"]] if pd.get("workspace") else []), "member": pd.get("member"),
                "starred_by": [], "stamp": not nostamp, "revisions": []}
        d["title"] = a.title
        if a.source and not d.get("source"):
            d["source"] = os.path.abspath(a.source)
        d["revisions"].append({"rev": rev, "file": rel, "date": date.isoformat(), "from": getattr(a, "origin", None) or src, "fingerprint": fp,
                               "sha256": sha, "stamped": how, "pages": pages(dst), "bytes": os.path.getsize(dst),
                               "filed_at": datetime.datetime.now(datetime.timezone.utc).strftime("%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ")})
        for k, v in (("note", (a.note or "").strip() or None), ("describes", describes), ("cost", cost)):
            if v:
                d["revisions"][-1][k] = v
        save(reg)
        write_views(reg, set(d["visibility"]) - {"owner"})
    print(f"{full}\t{dst}\tfiled")
    return 0


def cmd_number(a):
    describes = check_describes(a.describes)
    with Lock():
        reg = load()
        proj, num, d, rev = plan(reg, a)   # a project it would create is not saved: `number` reserves nothing
    full = f"{num}-{rev}"
    if a.tex:
        st = " · ".join([full] + ([describes] if describes else []) + [stampdate(datetime.date.today())])
        print(f"\\def\\docnumber{{{full}}}\\def\\docstamp{{{st}}}")
    else:
        print(full)
    return 0


def cmd_project(a):
    with Lock():
        reg = load()
        p = make_project(reg, a.name, a.number, a.kind, a.member)
        save(reg)
    d = reg["projects"][p]
    print(f"{p}\t{d['name']}\t{d['kind']}" + (f"\t{d['member']}" if d.get("member") else ""))
    return 0


def search(reg, query):
    """-> [(docnum, rev-or-None)] best matches for a number or words."""
    q = " ".join(query).strip()
    m = NUM.match(q)
    if m:
        num = f"{m.group(1)}-{m.group(2)}"
        return [(num, m.group(3))] if num in reg["documents"] else []
    words = [w for w in re.findall(r"[a-z0-9]+", q.lower()) if w not in STOP]
    if not words:
        return []
    scored = []
    for num, d in reg["documents"].items():
        if d["title"].lower() == q.lower():
            scored.append((100, num))
            continue
        hay = set(re.findall(r"[a-z0-9]+", " ".join([d["title"], reg["projects"].get(d["project"], {}).get("name", ""),
                                                     d.get("source") or ""]).lower()))
        tw = set(re.findall(r"[a-z0-9]+", d["title"].lower()))
        hit = sum(1 for w in words if w in hay)
        if hit == len(words):
            scored.append((hit + sum(1 for w in words if w in tw) / 10, num))
    if not scored:
        return []
    top = max(s for s, _ in scored)
    return [(n, None) for s, n in sorted(scored) if s == top]


def cmd_find(a):
    reg = load()
    hits = search(reg, a.query)
    if not hits:
        print(f"cc-docs: no document matches {' '.join(a.query)!r}", file=sys.stderr)
        return 1
    if len(hits) > 1:
        for n, _ in hits:
            print(f"{n}-{current(reg['documents'][n])['rev']}\t{reg['documents'][n]['title']}", file=sys.stderr)
        return 3
    n, rev = hits[0]
    d = reg["documents"][n]
    r = next((x for x in d["revisions"] if x["rev"] == rev), None) if rev else current(d)
    if not r:
        print(f"cc-docs: {n} has no revision {rev}", file=sys.stderr)
        return 1
    print(os.path.join(ROOT, r["file"]))
    return 0


def cmd_list(a):
    reg = load()
    proj = find_project(reg, a.project) if a.project else None
    if a.project and not proj:
        print(f"cc-docs: no project {a.project!r}", file=sys.stderr)
        return 1
    for n in sorted(reg["documents"]):
        d = reg["documents"][n]
        if proj and d["project"] != proj:
            continue
        r = current(d)
        print(f"{n}-{r['rev']}\t{r['date']}\towner{'+' + d['member'] if d.get('member') else ''}\t{d['title']}")
    return 0


def check_describes(b):
    if b and not BOARD.match(b):
        raise Refused(f"--describes {b!r} is not a board revision like PCB-0001-B")
    return b or None


def parse_cost(items):
    """--cost step=usd, once per step -> {"total", "steps": [{"step", "usd"}]} in the order given, or None."""
    steps = []
    for it in items or ():
        step, _, usd = it.partition("=")
        step = step.strip().lower()
        try:
            v = float(usd)
        except ValueError:
            v = -1.0
        if not STEP.match(step) or not 0 <= v < 1e6 or any(x["step"] == step for x in steps):
            raise Refused(f"--cost {it!r} is not one step=usd (e.g. draft=0.80), each step once")
        steps.append({"step": step, "usd": round(v, 4)})
    return {"total": round(sum(x["usd"] for x in steps), 4), "steps": steps} if steps else None


def viewer_ok(v):
    if v != "owner" and not WID.match(v or ""):
        raise Refused(f"no viewer {v!r}: the owner, or a member's workspace id")
    return v


def visible(d, viewer):
    return viewer == "owner" or viewer in d.get("visibility", ())


def starred_by(d):
    """Viewer ids that starred d. A document filed before stars were per viewer holds `starred`, the owner's."""
    return list(d.get("starred_by") or (["owner"] if d.get("starred") else []))


def get_rev(reg, full):
    m = NUM.match(full or "")
    d = reg["documents"].get(f"{m.group(1)}-{m.group(2)}") if m and m.group(3) else None
    r = next((x for x in d["revisions"] if x["rev"] == m.group(3)), None) if d else None
    if not r:
        raise Refused(f"no revision {full!r}: give PPP-NNNN-R")
    return d, r


def cmd_star(a):
    viewer = viewer_ok(a.viewer)
    with Lock():
        reg = load()
        d = reg["documents"].get(a.number)
        if not d or not visible(d, viewer):   # a document the viewer cannot see answers as one that does not exist
            raise Refused(f"no document {a.number!r}")
        who = [v for v in starred_by(d) if v != viewer] + ([viewer] if a.state == "on" else [])
        d["starred_by"] = sorted(who)
        d.pop("starred", None)
        save(reg)
        write_views(reg, set(d["visibility"]) - {"owner"})
    print(f"{a.number}\t{'starred' if a.state == 'on' else 'not starred'}")
    return 0


def cmd_public(a):
    with Lock():
        reg = load()
        d, r = get_rev(reg, a.number)
        if a.state == "on":
            # brief: "going public mints an unguessable token for exactly one revision"
            r.setdefault("public_token", secrets.token_urlsafe(24))
        else:
            # brief: "going private deletes it for good"
            r.pop("public_token", None)
        d.pop("public", None)
        save(reg)
        write_views(reg, set(d["visibility"]) - {"owner"})
    print(r.get("public_token") or "private")
    return 0


def public_file(reg, token, full):
    """The filed copy a public link serves, or None: the token must be that one revision's, and still held."""
    try:
        d, r = get_rev(reg, full)
    except Refused:
        return None
    held = r.get("public_token") or ""
    return os.path.join(ROOT, r["file"]) if held and secrets.compare_digest(held, token) else None


def cmd_token(a):
    f = public_file(load(), a.token, a.number)
    if f:
        print(f)
    return 0 if f else 1


_PAGE_COUNTS = {}


def _pages(f):
    """pages(), remembered: a filed copy is never rewritten, and a revision filed before `pages` was recorded
    would otherwise cost a pdfinfo on every library() a long-running caller makes."""
    if f not in _PAGE_COUNTS:
        _PAGE_COUNTS[f] = pages(f)
    return _PAGE_COUNTS[f]


def library(reg, viewer):
    """What `viewer` may see, and nothing else: a member never gets another workspace's document, project, star
    or any public token."""
    owner = viewer == "owner"
    host = os.uname().nodename
    home = os.path.expanduser("~")
    docs = []
    for n in sorted(reg["documents"]):
        d = reg["documents"][n]
        if not visible(d, viewer) or not d["revisions"]:
            continue
        revs = []
        for r in d["revisions"]:
            f = os.path.join(ROOT, r["file"])
            out = {"rev": r["rev"], "date": r["date"], "note": r.get("note"), "file": f"/files/{n}-{r['rev']}.pdf",
                   "pages": r.get("pages") or _pages(f), "bytes": r.get("bytes") or (os.path.getsize(f) if os.path.exists(f) else 0),
                   "describes": r.get("describes"), "cost": r.get("cost"),
                   "public": owner and bool(r.get("public_token"))}
            if owner and r.get("public_token"):
                out["token"] = r["public_token"]
            revs.append(out)
        src = d.get("source")
        if src and src.startswith(home + "/"):
            src = "~" + src[len(home):]
        docs.append({"number": n, "project": d["project"], "title": d["title"], "current": d["revisions"][-1]["rev"],
                     "starred": viewer in starred_by(d), "access": list(d.get("visibility", ["owner"])),
                     "source": f"{host}:{src}" if src else None, "revisions": revs})
    projs = sorted({d["project"] for d in docs} | (set(reg["projects"]) if owner else set()))
    return {"viewer": {"id": viewer, "role": "owner" if owner else "member"},
            "projects": [{"number": p, "name": reg["projects"][p]["name"]} for p in projs],
            "documents": docs}


def cmd_library(a):
    json.dump(library(load(), viewer_ok(a.viewer)), sys.stdout, indent=1)
    print()
    return 0


def retire_record(reg, key, entry, why):
    """Keep what a fold or a retire takes out as retired/<key>.json, and mark a document number as never reused."""
    os.makedirs(os.path.join(ROOT, "retired"), mode=0o700, exist_ok=True)
    at = datetime.datetime.now(datetime.timezone.utc).strftime("%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ")
    fd, tmp = tempfile.mkstemp(dir=os.path.join(ROOT, "retired"), prefix=".retired.")
    with os.fdopen(fd, "w") as f:
        json.dump(dict(why, at=at, entry=entry), f, indent=1, sort_keys=True)
        f.write("\n")
    os.replace(tmp, os.path.join(ROOT, "retired", key + ".json"))
    if NUM.match(key) and not NUM.match(key).group(3):
        reg.setdefault("retired", {})[key] = dict(why, at=at)


def prune_views(wids, rels):
    """Take the filed copies at rels out of each view, before write_views links what the register now holds."""
    for wid in wids:
        for rel in rels:
            f = os.path.join(ROOT, "ws", wid, rel)
            if os.path.lexists(f):
                os.unlink(f)


def get_doc(reg, num):
    m = NUM.match(num or "")
    d = reg["documents"].get(num) if m and not m.group(3) else None
    if not d:
        raise Refused(f"no document {num!r}: give PPP-NNNN")
    return d


def cmd_fold(a):
    with Lock():
        reg = load()
        keep = get_doc(reg, a.keep)
        others = [get_doc(reg, n) for n in a.other]
        docs = [keep] + others
        if len({d["number"] for d in docs}) != len(docs):
            raise Refused("a document is named twice")
        if any(d["project"] != keep["project"] for d in others):
            raise Refused(f"every document must be under {keep['number']}'s project {keep['project']}")
        if any(d.get("retired_revs") for d in docs):
            raise Refused("a document with a retired revision cannot be folded: its letter would be handed out again")
        # brief: "ordered oldest first by revision date (ties go by the order given) ... its current revision must
        # stay the newest, so the next build of its source still matches it"
        last = current(keep)
        rest = sorted(((r["date"], i, j, d, r) for i, d in enumerate(docs) for j, r in enumerate(d["revisions"])
                       if r is not last), key=lambda x: x[:3])
        late = [f"{d['number']}-{r['rev']}" for dt, _, _, d, r in rest if dt > last["date"]]
        if late:
            raise Refused(f"{', '.join(late)} is dated after {keep['number']}-{last['rev']}, which must stay the newest")
        order = [(d, r) for *_, d, r in rest] + [(keep, last)]
        slug = slugify(keep["title"])
        moves, revs = [], []
        for i, (d, r) in enumerate(order):
            new = dict(r, rev=letter(i), file=os.path.join("files", keep["project"], f"{keep['number']}-{letter(i)}_{slug}.pdf"))
            if (d is not keep or r["rev"] != new["rev"]) and new.pop("public_token", None):
                print(f"{d['number']}-{r['rev']}\tits public link stops working", file=sys.stderr)
            if d is not keep:
                new["folded_from"] = f"{d['number']}-{r['rev']}"
            moves.append((f"{d['number']}-{r['rev']}", r["file"], new["file"]))
            revs.append(new)
        old = {o for _, o, _ in moves}
        missing = [o for o in old if not os.path.isfile(os.path.join(ROOT, o))]
        clash = [n for *_, n in moves if n not in old and os.path.lexists(os.path.join(ROOT, n))]
        if missing or clash:
            raise Refused(f"{(missing + clash)[0]} is {'missing' if missing else 'in the way'}; nothing changed")
        for d in others:
            retire_record(reg, d["number"], d, {"folded_into": keep["number"]})
        # every copy steps aside to a temporary name first, since a new name may be an old one still in place
        for k, (_, o, n) in enumerate(moves):
            os.rename(os.path.join(ROOT, o), os.path.join(ROOT, n + f".fold{k}"))
        for k, (_, o, n) in enumerate(moves):
            os.rename(os.path.join(ROOT, n + f".fold{k}"), os.path.join(ROOT, n))
        keep["revisions"] = revs
        wids = set().union(*(set(d.get("visibility", ())) for d in docs)) - {"owner"}
        for d in others:
            del reg["documents"][d["number"]]
        save(reg)
        prune_views(wids, old)
        write_views(reg, wids)
    for (was, _, n), r in zip(moves, revs):
        print(f"{was}\t{keep['number']}-{r['rev']}\t{os.path.join(ROOT, n)}")
    return 0


def cmd_retire(a):
    with Lock():
        reg = load()
        m = NUM.match(a.number or "")
        if m and m.group(3):
            d, r = get_rev(reg, a.number)
            gone = d["revisions"] if len(d["revisions"]) == 1 else [r]
        else:
            d = get_doc(reg, a.number)
            gone = d["revisions"]
        whole = gone is d["revisions"]
        key = d["number"] if whole else a.number
        retire_record(reg, key, d if whole else r, {"retired": key})
        for x in gone:
            dst = os.path.join(ROOT, "retired", x["file"])
            os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(dst), exist_ok=True)
            os.rename(os.path.join(ROOT, x["file"]), dst)
        if whole:
            del reg["documents"][d["number"]]
        else:
            d["revisions"].remove(r)
            d.setdefault("retired_revs", []).append(r["rev"])
        save(reg)
        wids = set(d.get("visibility", ())) - {"owner"}
        prune_views(wids, [x["file"] for x in gone])
        write_views(reg, wids)
    for x in gone:
        print(f"{d['number']}-{x['rev']}\tretired\t{os.path.join(ROOT, 'retired', x['file'])}")
    return 0


# ── selfcheck ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# ── a member workspace files across its socket ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Inside a member's sandbox ~/.cc/documents is that member's read-only view, so `file` and `number` there cannot
# write. They cross the workspace's own socket instead (across), as `cc-mail send` does: the daemon's member verb
# `docs` runs `cc-docs member <handle>` on the host with the handle it read off the socket, and member_ask decides.
HOME = os.path.expanduser("~")
SLACKSOCK = os.path.join(os.environ.get("CC_SLACK_DIR") or os.path.join(HOME, ".cc", "slack"), "sock")
IN_SANDBOX = os.environ.get("CC_MEMBER_SANDBOX") == "1"
MEMBER_CAP = 64 << 20     # the largest PDF a workspace may file, in bytes
MEMBER_WAIT = 300         # seconds the workspace waits on the host: stamping and printing a long PDF takes a while
HANDLE = re.compile(r"^[a-z0-9][a-z0-9-]{0,39}$")
ASK = {"op", "pdf", "title", "project", "source", "kind", "member", "describes", "note", "date", "cost", "no_stamp", "tex"}


def across(a):
    """`file` or `number` inside a member workspace: the flags as an ask on the member socket, the host's line back."""
    import socket
    ask = {"op": a.cmd, "title": a.title}
    for k in ("project", "kind", "member", "describes", "note", "date", "cost"):
        if getattr(a, k, None):
            ask[k] = getattr(a, k)
    if a.source:
        ask["source"] = os.path.abspath(a.source)
    if a.cmd == "file":
        ask["pdf"] = os.path.abspath(a.pdf)
        ask["no_stamp"] = bool(a.no_stamp)
    else:
        ask["tex"] = bool(a.tex)
    c = socket.socket(socket.AF_UNIX, socket.SOCK_STREAM)
    c.settimeout(MEMBER_WAIT)
    try:
        c.connect(SLACKSOCK)
        c.sendall((json.dumps({"docs": ask}) + "\n").encode())
        buf = b""
        while not buf.endswith(b"\n"):
            d = c.recv(65536)
            if not d:
                break
            buf += d
        answer = json.loads(buf or b"{}")
    except Exception as e:
        print(f"cc-docs: nothing filed — the workspace's socket did not answer ({str(e)[:200]}): the host files for "
              "this workspace, and nothing there is listening", file=sys.stderr)
        return 1
    if isinstance(answer, dict) and answer.get("ok"):
        print(str(answer.get("text") or ""))
        return 0
    print(f"cc-docs: {(answer.get('error') if isinstance(answer, dict) else '') or 'the host refused'}", file=sys.stderr)
    return 2


def member_trees(handle, files):
    """The directories a workspace may file from, resolved: its ~/dev/<h>, its track worktrees and its Slack files."""
    return [os.path.realpath(p) for p in (os.path.join(HOME, "dev", handle),
                                          os.path.join(HOME, ".cc", "worktrees", handle), files) if p]


def within(path, trees):
    return any(path == t or path.startswith(t.rstrip("/") + "/") for t in trees)


def member_pdf(path, trees):
    """The bytes of a workspace's PDF, read from ONE fd: O_NOFOLLOW refuses a link as the last part, the fd's own
    /proc path must be inside the workspace (which catches a linked directory), and the read stops past the cap —
    so the file cannot be swapped between the check and the read (outbound.attach_bytes, the same reasoning)."""
    nope = f"{path} is not a file inside this workspace"
    try:
        fd = os.open(path, os.O_RDONLY | os.O_NOFOLLOW | os.O_CLOEXEC)
    except OSError:
        raise Refused(nope)
    try:
        st = os.fstat(fd)
        try:
            real = os.readlink(f"/proc/self/fd/{fd}")
        except OSError:
            raise Refused(nope)
        if not stat.S_ISREG(st.st_mode) or real.endswith(" (deleted)") or not within(real, trees):
            raise Refused(nope)
        if st.st_size > MEMBER_CAP:
            raise Refused(f"{path} is {st.st_size >> 20} MiB; a workspace files a PDF of {MEMBER_CAP >> 20} MiB at most")
        data = b""
        while len(data) <= MEMBER_CAP:
            chunk = os.read(fd, 1 << 20)
            if not chunk:
                break
            data += chunk
    finally:
        os.close(fd)
    if len(data) > MEMBER_CAP:
        raise Refused(f"{path} grew past {MEMBER_CAP >> 20} MiB while it was read")
    if not data.startswith(b"%PDF-"):
        raise Refused(f"{path} is not a PDF; a workspace files PDFs only")
    return data


def member_project(reg, handle, named):
    """-> (project, kind, member) for plan(). The workspace's own project is the one its ask names when that one is
    its own, else its first; a workspace with none gets one named after it. Another member's project is refused.
    An owner project named from a workspace is not the workspace's to file into, so its own takes its place: a
    maker that set DOC_PROJECT for the host still files, under the member."""
    p = find_project(reg, named) if named else None
    if p and reg["projects"][p].get("member") == handle:
        return p, None, None
    if p and reg["projects"][p].get("member"):
        raise Refused(f"project {named!r} is another member's; a workspace files only under its own")
    own = sorted(q for q, d in reg["projects"].items() if d.get("member") == handle)
    if own:
        return own[0], None, None
    if find_project(reg, handle):
        raise Refused(f"project {handle!r} is not this workspace's, and it has none of its own to file under")
    return handle, "member", handle


def member_ask(handle, ask, files=""):
    """One workspace's `file` or `number`, decided on the host. `handle` is the daemon's, read off the socket the ask
    came on, and never the ask's; the ask may name its PDF, title, source, note, date, cost, board revision and
    whether to stamp. -> the line `file` or `number` prints. Refused: another member's project or --member, a PDF
    or source outside the workspace's own trees, anything but a PDF, one over MEMBER_CAP, any op but these two."""
    import argparse
    import contextlib
    import io
    # brief: "The host files only into the project that belongs to the asking workspace, identified by the socket,
    # never by anything the workspace says." `handle` is the socket's; the ask's `member` can only agree with it.
    if not HANDLE.match(handle or ""):
        raise Refused(f"no workspace {handle!r}")
    if not isinstance(ask, dict):
        raise Refused("docs wants one object")
    odd = sorted(str(k)[:40] for k in set(ask) - ASK)
    if odd:
        raise Refused(f"unknown key {', '.join(odd)} — the keys are {', '.join(sorted(ASK))}")
    op = ask.get("op")
    if op not in ("file", "number"):
        raise Refused(f"a workspace can file and number its documents, not {str(op)[:40]!r}; only the owner makes "
                      "anything public, stars for someone else, or makes a project")
    title, cost = ask.get("title"), ask.get("cost") or []
    if not isinstance(title, str) or not title.strip():
        raise Refused("a document needs a title")
    if not isinstance(cost, list) or not all(isinstance(c, str) for c in cost):
        raise Refused("cost is a list of <step>=<usd>")
    for k in ("project", "kind", "member", "describes", "note", "date", "source", "pdf"):
        if ask.get(k) is not None and not isinstance(ask[k], str):
            raise Refused(f"{k} must be a string")
    if ask.get("member") and ask["member"] != handle:
        raise Refused(f"a workspace files only for itself, not for {ask['member'][:40]!r}")
    inside = os.path.join(HOME, ".cc", "slack", "files") + "/"
    here = lambda q: os.path.join(files, q[len(inside):]) if files and q.startswith(inside) else q   # the boundary's ~/.cc/slack is the member dir
    trees = member_trees(handle, files)
    source = ask.get("source")
    if source and not within(os.path.normpath(here(source)), trees):
        raise Refused(f"{source} is not a path inside this workspace")
    tmp = None
    try:
        if op == "file":
            data = member_pdf(here(str(ask.get("pdf") or "")), trees)
            os.makedirs(ROOT, mode=0o700, exist_ok=True)
            tmp = tempfile.mkdtemp(dir=ROOT, prefix=".incoming.")
            pdf = os.path.join(tmp, "in.pdf")
            with open(pdf, "wb") as f:
                f.write(data)
        a = argparse.Namespace(cmd=op, title=title.strip(), source=source or None, describes=ask.get("describes"),
                               note=ask.get("note"), date=ask.get("date"), cost=cost, no_stamp=bool(ask.get("no_stamp")),
                               tex=bool(ask.get("tex")), origin=ask.get("pdf"), pdf=pdf if op == "file" else None)
        with Lock():
            a.project, a.kind, a.member = member_project(load(), handle, ask.get("project"))
        out = io.StringIO()
        with contextlib.redirect_stdout(out):
            (cmd_file if op == "file" else cmd_number)(a)
        return out.getvalue().strip()
    finally:
        if tmp:
            shutil.rmtree(tmp, ignore_errors=True)


def cmd_member(a):
    """The daemon's half of the member verb `docs`: the ask as JSON on stdin, the answer as JSON on stdout."""
    try:
        ask = json.loads(sys.stdin.read() or "null")
        print(json.dumps({"ok": True, "text": member_ask(a.handle, ask, a.files or "")}))
        return 0
    except (Refused, ValueError) as e:
        print(json.dumps({"ok": False, "error": str(e)}))
        return 2


def selfcheck():
    global ROOT, MEMBERS, HOME, IN_SANDBOX, SLACKSOCK, MEMBER_CAP
    n = [0, 0]

    def ok(name, cond):
        n[0 if cond else 1] += 1
        print(("  ok   " if cond else "  FAIL ") + name)

    def mkpdf(d, name, body):
        """A one-page PDF saying `body`, built by pdflatex in d."""
        with open(os.path.join(d, name + ".tex"), "w") as f:
            f.write("\\documentclass{article}\\pagestyle{empty}\\begin{document}" + body + "\\end{document}\n")
        subprocess.run(["pdflatex", "-interaction=batchmode", name + ".tex"], cwd=d, capture_output=True)
        return os.path.join(d, name + ".pdf")

    def run(*args):
        out, err = sys.stdout, sys.stderr
        import io
        sys.stdout, sys.stderr = io.StringIO(), io.StringIO()
        try:
            rc = main(list(args))
        finally:
            o, e = sys.stdout.getvalue(), sys.stderr.getvalue()
            sys.stdout, sys.stderr = out, err
        return rc, o + e

    print("cc-docs selfcheck")
    ok("letters: A, H→J (I skipped), N→P (O skipped), Z, then AA", [letter(i) for i in (0, 8, 13, 23, 24, 25)]
       == ["A", "J", "P", "Z", "AA", "AB"])
    ok("slug: lowercase with hyphens", slugify("The Autobox: Explanation (v2)") == "the-autobox-explanation-v2")
    with tempfile.TemporaryDirectory(prefix="cc-docs-sc-") as t:
        src = os.path.join(t, "src")
        os.makedirs(src)
        MEMBERS = os.path.join(t, "members")
        wid = "0123456789abcdef"
        os.makedirs(os.path.join(MEMBERS, "kid1"))
        with open(os.path.join(MEMBERS, "kid1", "workspace-id"), "w") as f:
            f.write(wid + "\n")
        # numbering: each case files into a register of its own
        ROOT = os.path.join(t, "r1")
        a = mkpdf(src, "a", "Alpha one")
        b = mkpdf(src, "b", "Beta one\\newpage Beta two\\newpage Beta three")
